📖 Project Overview

BMI Predictor is an end-to-end machine learning system that forecasts patients’ future Body Mass Index (BMI) values using historical EMR data.
The project leverages multiple regression and ensemble models to predict BMI changes, detect trends, and provide explainability for healthcare insights.

It integrates a Flask backend (for model inference and data handling) with a React frontend (for interactive result visualization, including prediction trends, metrics, and SHAP-based interpretability).

🎯 Problem Statement

Body Mass Index (BMI) is a vital sign tracked in EMRs and is a key indicator of overall health, risk of comorbidities, and treatment effectiveness.
Modeling its change over time enables proactive and personalized healthcare interventions.

Objective:
Develop a machine learning model to predict future BMI values or trends using routinely available EMR features (vitals, diagnoses, medications, procedures, etc.).

Deliverables:

A trained ML model to predict future BMI values/trends.

A demo application showing predictions, actual labels, and explanations.

A detailed report and presentation of the full ML lifecycle — from literature review to evaluation.

✨ Features
🧠 BMI Forecasting

Predicts future BMI values and change trends for each patient.

Displays actual vs predicted BMI in the frontend.

📊 Metrics & Visualization

Automatic generation of:

R² Score, MAE, MAPE, RMSE, MSE, MSLE, RMSLE

Classification metrics (F1, Precision, Recall, Accuracy, AUROC)

Interactive graphs:

SHAP Explanation Curves

Feature Importance

Confusion Matrix

Calibration Curve

💾 Data Handling

Data extracted directly from CureMD’s EMR MongoDB dataset.

Preprocessing pipeline ensures consistency, removes outliers, and fixes incorrect entries in vitals and medication data.

💡 Explainability

SHAP (SHapley Additive exPlanations) for model interpretation.

Feature importance plots for model transparency.

🧠 ML Models & Approach

The project implements and compares multiple regression and ensemble models:

Category	Algorithms Used
Linear Models	Ridge Regression, Lasso Regression, Elastic Net
Tree-Based	Random Forest, Gradient Boosting, XGBoost

Each model was tuned and evaluated using cross-validation to ensure robustness and fairness.

📈 Model Evaluation & Metrics

Regression Metrics:

R² Score

Mean Absolute Error (MAE)

Mean Absolute Percentage Error (MAPE)

Mean Squared Error (MSE)

Root Mean Squared Error (RMSE)

Mean Squared Log Error (MSLE)

Root Mean Squared Log Error (RMSLE)

Classification Metrics (for change prediction):

Accuracy

Precision

Recall

F1 Score

AUROC

Visual Evaluation:

SHAP Value Plots (Explainability)

Confusion Matrix

Calibration Curves

Feature Importance Charts

🛠️ Tech Stack

Backend:

Flask (Python)

Scikit-Learn, XGBoost, NumPy, Pandas, SHAP, Matplotlib

Frontend:

React.js, Tailwind CSS, Chart.js / Plotly (for metrics visualization)

Data Source:

MongoDB EMR dataset from CureMD

Deployment Ready:

Modular Flask API

React interface with dynamic API integration